Subject: [PATCH] Cancel socket I/O and handle TCP EOF during connection teardown

Base: alvr-org/ALVR e8ca92b15d7c93765f828ca245f26de678c7f154
Related: https://github.com/alvr-org/ALVR/issues/3190

Do not force Disconnecting back to Disconnected while old workers still exist.
Handle EOF and fragmented prefixes without spinning, interrupt blocking I/O
before joining workers, and release state locks before acquiring sender locks.
The shared socket changes and client teardown also apply to Android builds.

